#
# Mustfile — release-blocking invariants for sim-insolvency.
# Verb:      must
# Authority: hard (a violated must blocks release)
#
# Declaration only — see ../INDEX.a2ml on shape. The `run` line of each check is
# the REAL command that enforces it today, so these are verifiable by hand even
# though no contractile runner executes this file.

@abstract:
What must hold for sim-insolvency to be releasable. The first group is the
product's reason to exist: if hidden scenario reality can reach a learner, the
assessment is void, and nothing else here matters.
@end

## Hidden truth

### hidden-reality-absent-from-artefacts
- description: No hidden scenario reality appears in the shipped bundle, the binary, or any runtime output.
- run: "./tools/check-hidden-truth.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: Deny-list is derived from scenarios/*/reality/reality.a2ml, so scenario authoring cannot drift out of sync. A vacuous derivation aborts rather than passing.

### hidden-truth-gate-can-fail
- description: The hidden-truth scanner is proved able to fail, once per channel.
- run: "./tools/test-hidden-truth-scanner.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: 9 canaries. A gate that cannot fail is not a gate; this check is what makes the one above meaningful.

### kernel-emits-no-hidden-truth
- description: Across all eight golden runs, no ledger event payload, actor or certificate contains a reality phrase.
- run: "zig build test"
- severity: blocker

## Ledger and result integrity

### ledger-replay-deterministic
- description: Golden runs replay to byte-identical digests, and a tampered ledger fails verification.
- run: "zig build test"
- severity: blocker

### abi-manifest-consistent
- description: AffineScript, Idris2, Zig and the neutral ABI manifest agree on version, status ordinals, ownership and proof shape.
- run: "./tools/check-abi-drift.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: WEAK — this check is grep-only and has no canary suite. It cannot detect semantic drift. Recorded in docs/KNOWN-DEBT.adoc.

### scenario-structure-valid
- description: The scenario carries its required files, neutral evidence and route fixtures, and the learner bundle passes its leak checks.
- run: "./tools/validate-scenario.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: No canary suite. See docs/KNOWN-DEBT.adoc.

## Stack and licence

### prohibited-stack-absent
- description: No Python, TypeScript, JavaScript, C/C++, React, Electron/Tauri scaffold or Nix flake.
- run: "./tools/check-no-prohibited-stack.sh"
- severity: blocker

### spdx-present
- description: Every source and data file carries an SPDX-License-Identifier of PMPL-2.0-or-later.
- run: "grep -rL 'SPDX-License-Identifier' --include='*.zig' --include='*.idr' --include='*.a2ml' --include='*.adoc' ."
- severity: blocker
- notes: Shebang and doctype lines take precedence over line-1 placement; see docs/KNOWN-DEBT.adoc for the ruling and the exceptions.

## Documentation

### wiki-register-consistent
- description: Every registered wiki page exists, carries its required metadata, has a unique page-id, and the page-register rows agree with the pages' own ids.
- run: "./tools/check-wiki-health.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: Runs in CI but is NOT a dependency of `just check`. See docs/KNOWN-DEBT.adoc (check-and-ci-diverge).

### wiki-gate-can-fail
- description: The wiki health gate is proved able to fail.
- run: "./tools/test-wiki-health.sh"
- severity: blocker
- notes: 3 canaries.

## Product boundary

### disclaimers-intact
- description: Every emitted artefact states that it is simulation output and not legal advice, a qualification, a JIEB result or accredited CPD.
- run: "./zig-out/bin/sim-insolvency certificate learner-pseudonym | grep -q 'disclaimer'"
- severity: blocker
- notes: The disclaimer is embedded in the certificate envelope and re-verified on import, not merely printed in documentation.
